e finished the report, but they was not ready to submit it. He don't know whether the weather will hold.\n\nA apple a day keeps the doctor away. An university is not a hotel, and an hour is not a long time. I think i am right about this.\n\nDue to the fact that the budget is limited, we will utilize existing tools. At this point in time, a large number of users prefer the older version.\n\nThe quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The the dog did not move , it just watched.\n\nMr. Jones arrived at 9 a.m. on Monday. He met Prof. Lee at the U.S. embassy, and they talked for 2.5 hours about Fig. 3 and Table 2.\n\nIn conclusion, the proposed approach is simple, fast and robust. Future work will focus on improving its ability to handle very long documents.\n\nTitle Without A Full Stop\nThis line follows a title-like line.\n\n- First item in a list\n- Second item, with a comma, and more words\n- Third item\n\n\"Quoted speech is tricky,\" she said. \"Is it not?\" He nodded.\n\nThe function returns None when the input is empty; otherwise it returns a list of tuples (start, end, text).\n\nVisit https://example.com/docs or write to someone@example.org for more information.\n\nThey didn't went home early. She has wrote three papers. We have ran the tests twice.\n\nThere are several reason for this. Many student find the topic hard. Each of the students have a laptop.\n\nIts a well known fact that more better tools give faster results.\n"],"out":[[56,67,"In order to"],[68,82,"make sure that"],[868,888,"Due to the fact that"],[944,965,"At this point in time"],[967,984,"a large number of"],[1242,1255,"In conclusion"],[1324,1332,"focus on"]]},{"args":["---\ntitle: Edge cases\ntags: [test, markdown]\n---\n\n# Heading one\n\nSetext heading\n==============\n\nSecond setext\n-------------\n\nA paragraph with **bold**, *italic*, ***both***, ~~struck~~, `code`, and a [link](https://example.com \"title\").\nAn autolink <https://rust-lang.org> and a bare www.example.com address. Inline